From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:36:28 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] autotests: The window stack layers and a chain of menus
 one limit per level

testStereoDepthStack: one to twelve windows (the layers, the first right
behind the screen, the sixth and the rest at the limit), a chain of one to four
menus in a plain window and in a window kept above the others (n limits from
the base, the parent unchanged when a sub-menu opens, each above its parent),
a dialog with a combo box's list or a menu and a sub-menu in it (plain and kept above), a dialog with a combo box's list or a menu and a sub-menu in it (plain
and kept above), and a sub-menu taller than the output room, which kept the screen's level
behind its parent. testStereoDepthPopups and testStereoDepthPinnedStack expect
one limit per level; testStereoDepthPinned, testStereoDepthMotion and
testQuickStereo expect the first layer of a window beneath the active one
instead of the limit.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
